<title>USA: Reebok International Inc Q3 net falls.</title>
<headline>Reebok International Inc Q3 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>STOUGHTON, Mass 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.75		    $0.96</p>
<p> Net			 50,612		   76,202</p>
<p> Revs		     970,080		1,005,980</p>
<p> Avg			 67,839		   79,304</p>
<p>	  9  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.64		    $2.03</p>
<p> Net			118,840		  163,523</p>
<p> Revs		   2,690,575		2,730,150</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  72,422		   80,602</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Revs include $36.3 million in Q3 1995, $104.1 million in nine months 1995, and $49.4 million nine months 1996 from Avia subsidiary, sold in June 1996.</p>
<p>Nine months 1995 includes Q2 special charge of $11.2 million after taxes, or $0.14 per share, for facilities consolidation, severance and other expenses from business re-engineering activities.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610</p>
